<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Home-screen hero infographic.
      - Phone (left, emerald): 88x188, ~9:19 portrait aspect like a real phone.
      - TV (right, blue): 174x98, ~16:9 landscape aspect like a real flat-panel.
      - Wi-Fi hub: centered between them at (132, 97).
      - Connection: faint dashed line from phone -> hub -> TV, with three blue
        data dots traveling along it on a continuous loop. Dots get visually
        absorbed by the hub disc as they pass through (z-order — dots drawn
        before the hub, so the hub covers them in the middle).
      - Both phone and TV screens render the SAME sunset scene (sky + mountains
        + glowing sun + stars). The two suns share the sun_pulse animator so
        they breathe in lockstep, telling the user "same content on both".
    Animation wired up in avd_phone_tv_cast.xml.
-->
